<Legal
  title="Data Processing Addendum"
  description="For customers who need a DPA to satisfy their own GDPR obligations — e.g. a Team plan admin."
  lastUpdated="2026-08-07"
>
  <p>
    If your organization needs a signed Data Processing Addendum to satisfy its own GDPR
    obligations when using Porphyra (most relevant once our Team plan ships — see
    <a href="/pricing">pricing</a>), this page describes what it will cover. A signable
    version will be available from account settings once billing supports organizational
    accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>Roles</h2>
  <p>
    For personal accounts, you are the data controller of your own CV and application data;
    Porphyra is the processor. For organizational accounts (once available), the
    organization is the controller for data it manages on behalf of its members.
  </p>

  <h2>Subprocessors</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/legal/subprocessors">subprocessors list</a> — the full DPA incorporates
    it by reference and commits to advance notice before adding a new one.
  </p>

  <h2>Security measures</h2>
  <p>
    Summarized on our <a href="/security">security page</a>: client-side E2EE for content
    data, consented and non-persisted plaintext processing for AI evaluation, encrypted
    backups, and the access controls described in our security documentation.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Where data is transferred outside the EEA/UK (e.g. to a US-based AI provider for a
    consented evaluation), we rely on Standard Contractual Clauses or an equivalent
    safeguard, per subprocessor — detailed per-entry on the subprocessors page.
  </p>

  <h2>Requesting a signed copy</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:privacy@porphyra.example">privacy@porphyra.example</a>.</p>
</Legal>
